  "outlook_text": "ESAB raised its full year 2023 outlook and expects core organic sales growth of 3.5% to 5.5%, total core sales growth of 4.0% to 6.0%, core adjusted EBITDA of $430 to $450 million, and core adjusted EPS of $3.85 to $4.05, up from our prior guidance of core organic sales growth of 3.0% to 5.0%, total core sales growth of 2.0% to 4.0%, core adjusted EBITDA of $420 to $440 million and core adjusted EPS of $3.80 to $4.00. [Outlook table] ESAB 2023 Outlook ; Previous Guidance | New Guidance ; 2022 Core net sales | 2,429.9 | 2,429.9 ; Organic growth | 3%-5% | 3.5%-5.5% ; Acquisitions | 2.5% | 2.5% ; Currency | (3.5)% | (2.0)% ; 2023 Core net sales growth range | 2%-4% | 4%-6% ; 2022 Core adjusted EBITDA | 408.4 | 408.4 ; 2023 Core adjusted EBITDA range | $ 420-$ 440 | $ 430-$ 450",
  "notes_on_special_items": "Adj. NI pretax items: restructuring 9.4 (incl. impairment of long-lived assets), acquisition-amortization and other related charges 9.3, separation costs 0; tax effect (4.2); discrete tax adjustments +19.6 (net discrete tax expenses re dividend withholding tax and unrecognized tax benefits from adverse foreign court ruling). Adj. FCF adds back Separation payments 4.4 and discontinued ops 5.3."
